    pnp: share pinned corpus across gap attempts via hardlinks
    
    assignment.prepare() used git worktree add to check out a full ~446 MB
    pinned corpus for every new gap attempt, so reclaimed disk refilled and
    the box projected full before the 24h restart. Reuse one preserved central
    corpus per pinned base and hardlink byte-identical tracked files into each
    attempt; new/mutated files stay per-attempt. Shared files are immutable so
    an in-place edit cannot corrupt peers. Best-effort with full-checkout
    fallback. Offline test covers dedup, new-file isolation and clean git state.

